  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Partnership for Output Based Aid (GPOBA) Department for International Development (DFID) (Phase 2) Trust Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The main objectives are mainstreaming and implementing OBA by  Governments and Development Agencies as a key mechanism for improving  the lives of poor people by facilitating their access to affordable  infrastructure services.
 
 
 The priority countries for subsidies will be in Sub-Saharan Africa and  Asia with DFID&apos;s continued support in infrastructure services in  mature sectors such as energy and water &amp; sanitation, as well as less  mature ones such as public transport, solid waste and irrigation.    DFID funds have to be used at least 60% on Low Income Countries  (LIC) and 40% in Middle Income Countries (MIC).&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
